    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d893">

                <pb facs="1039" n="959" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg959"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch of May 31, 1902, reporting your reception as ambassador extraordinary
                    of the United States on a special mission to attend the ceremonies on the
                    occasion of the coming of age of Alphonso XIII.</p>
                <p>The Department is gratified to learn of the appreciative reception accorded to
                    you, as a forecast of the good will which this Government trusts will ever
                    prevail between the United States and Spain.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
